*.old
.tmp/
tmp/
scratch/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only tests and corpora (not tracked in the public repository)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: this must be `tests/*`, not `tests/`. Git will not re-include a path
# inside a directory that is itself excluded, so an excluded `tests/` makes the
# `!tests/corpus/` negation below a no-op and the benchmark corpus silently
# disappears from CI checkouts.
tests/*
# The accuracy-regression corpus IS tracked: the benchmark harness and the
# `benchmark` CI job cannot run without it. See docs/BENCHMARKING.md.
!tests/corpus/
# The integration suite and its fixtures ARE tracked -- `tests/integration_tests.rs`
# and 14 fixtures under `tests/contracts/` were already committed, but the
# over-broad `tests/` rule above silently dropped 32 fixtures added afterwards,
# so `cargo test` could not pass on a fresh clone. Both are re-included here.
!tests/integration_tests.rs
!tests/contracts/
# The integration suite scans fixtures in test_contracts/ by explicit path, so
# the directory must be tracked. 11 of its 12 files were already committed; the
# blanket rule silently dropped the 12th, and `cargo test` could not pass on a
# fresh clone as a result. Same failure mode as the `tests/` rule above.
!test_contracts/
fuzz/corpus/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark harness
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pinned upstream repos cloned by `scripts/benchmark.sh --with-upstream`.
.bench-cache/
scripts/__pycache__/
